! AlAs for chi^(2)(-2w; w, w) -- the same crystal as `alas-raman.in` at a basis
! a second-order susceptibility can actually be compared in.
!
! `alas-raman.in`'s `ecutwfc = 10` is what its own phonon reference was run at
! and is far too small here: chi^(2) carries two energy denominators rather than
! one, so the basis reaches it twice. Measured on this cell at a 6x6x6 mesh, the
! static chi^xyz goes -66.3 pm/V at 10 Ry to **-75.8 at 30**, against the
! vendored Elk's -85.4 -- so the cutoff is worth 12% and moves toward the
! all-electron answer rather than away from it -- and then stops: 45 Ry gives
! -76.6, so 30 is converged and the residual 11% against Elk is the
! pseudopotential rather than the basis.
!
! `nosym`/`noinv` and an **unshifted** grid, for P24's reason: chi^abc is a polar
! rank-3 tensor, a symmetry-reduced wedge does not sum to the cell's until it is
! averaged over the point group, and a *shifted* Monkhorst-Pack grid is not
! closed under that group. The k-set here is only the density's; the tensor is
! evaluated on a denser mesh the caller builds.
!
! AlAs is zincblende and therefore non-centrosymmetric, which is the whole point
! of the case: chi^(2) vanishes identically in every centrosymmetric crystal and
! `si2-nosym.in` is the control that says so.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    prefix = 'alas'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.575, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 30.0
    nosym = .true.
    noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98  Al.pz-vbc.UPF
 As  74.92  As.pz-bhs.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
